.TH DANBY-BASEBALLPITCH 1
.SH NAME
danby-baseballpitch \- aerodynamic flight of a pitched baseball
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/baseballpitch
.SH MODEL
The ball starts at release height with selectable speed and angle.  Quadratic
drag opposes its velocity and spin produces a perpendicular Magnus force.  The
display follows the pitch for 0.55 seconds, approximately the flight to home
plate, unless it strikes the ground first.
.SH DISPLAY
The spatial plot is height against distance; the smaller plot is speed against
time.  Tracks alter speed, angle, drag, lift, spin, and gravity and immediately
repeat the pitch.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/plugin/baseballpitch.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR trajectory (2)
